  "reason": "Evidence: The top-4 configs all use multimodal + multiprofile + imagenet_vit_l, with the best being config_035 (scvi_n200 + transformer + weighted, acc=0.725). scvi_n200 has dominated as the RNA encoder, but PCA_n2000 has never been paired with the proven-best image/aggregation/fusion stack (VIT_L + transformer + weighted). Uncertainty: It is unclear whether a simpler linear encoder (PCA) could match or slightly exceed the learned VAE (scvi) in this high-capacity multimodal setting, possibly by reducing overfitting on the RNA branch. This experiment (config_024) directly tests that question by swapping only the RNA encoder in the best-performing pipeline. It is the best use of experiment 9 because it is the single highest-information test remaining: if PCA matches scvi, we confirm a cheaper alternative; if it falls short, we confirm scvi_n200 is essential and can spend the final experiment on a minor perturbation of config_035. Expected cost: PCA_n2000 avoids VAE training, so this should be moderately cheaper than config_035 (3.60 GPU hrs), estimated around 2.5–3.2 GPU hrs, keeping total budget well within range."
